A||||15||Jake2m4||Alright lets hear it...  Air horns.||||5||
Z||000000||Jake2m4||08-02-2001||01:06 AM||||     I'm looking for quality air horns for my car.  I'm tired of people pulling out in front of me and cutting me off.  Either bc they don't notice or care that I'm there.  Anyways, I want to be able to tell them, and maybe get them to take a frantic look thinking I'm a semi truck barreling down towards them.  And I can barely hear my stock horn when I'm driving.<BR>     I've been looking around.  I just want to know if anyone has experience in this area.  As is brand names or signs of quality to look for.  Just jumping into things can be expensive.  So info would be helpful.<BR>     I'm looking for something with a small compressor and at least two dif frequency horns.  I've heard of ones that play music and I think those could be amusing.<BR>     PS  I don't go around blarring my horn at every thing.  But there are situations where it is appropriate and I'd like something a little better suited for it.  I don't remember when the last time I used my horn was but I remember thinking I wished that is was louder.<P>Thanks<BR>Jake<P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTBro||08-02-2001||01:23 AM||||I had an air horn on one of my old cars.  It was an 86 Sunbird.  That sucker was loud!  It was one with a little compressor and two horns.  When I was hooking them up and testing them, I would honk it in my driveway and I would hear an echo from three streets down!  It was super loud!<P>But the horns didnt last long.  I made the mistake of mounting them facing up and so water and dirt got into them and screwed up the diaphragm.<P>If you get them, make sure they are made of metal... and face them towards the back of the car...  Maybe slant them down a little so watever dirt or water that goes in will fall back out...<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||08-02-2001||02:41 AM||||i use to have the air horn that you can get at autozone.  it was ok.   it came with a little compresser.  the thing i didn't lik was that it was to high pitched.  nothing like a semi...  more like a loud turmpit.<P>i dont know about faceing them backwards.  then you would be honking at your self.   under you hood faceing forward would be save enough for them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-02-2001||06:09 AM||||dont waste your money. the idiots that cut in front of you like that are usually in their own world with radio cranked so loud they wouldnt hear it any better anyway. Just ram em. At least that way theyll be in hospital or worse so I wont have to worry about them when I drive.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||08-02-2001||09:49 AM||||Dumb *** alarm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I had one in an old beater. <BR>Keep your stock horn and mount a separate button for the Air horn. Great for the idiots that like to drive and talk on the phone.||||reg||1
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-02-2001||09:55 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake_Dragon:<BR><B>Dumb *** alarm    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I had one in an old beater. <BR>Keep your stock horn and mount a separate button for the Air horn. Great for the idiots that like to drive and talk on the phone.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good idea!   I think I need to invest in one for my wifes car too hehe<P>we each travel 1hr to work each way (worse thing about living in the country) and at least 1 car a trip pulls out in front of us.. <P>gotta love the ones that hesitate then pulls out at the last minute and putts along.. or the ones that pull out in front of you to turn into the NEXT driveway (even though there are no cars behind you..so they could have safely waited)<P><BR>edited: darn typos  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
