Z||000010||Fierowrecker||08-03-2001||07:40 AM||||Hey Jake!<BR>I had a set of old truck air horns in the radiator area of my 84 2M4...<BR>I used an electric air pump and a small air tank to supply the air...<BR>People did jump when I hit the "rip cord" and sounded the horn, but usually, they would just get mad and flip me off for scairing them...<BR>People like that are air headed and don't care about the other drivers, especially the ones with nice small cars...<BR>But they get removed from the roads in the winter when I drive my 4X4 farm truck and they try to pull out in front of me on icy roads...<BR>Another thing you could do, mount a gun rack in the back window of your Fiero, and put NRA stickers in the windows, and my fav, Guns don't kill people, I do! sticker...<BR>Makes people think twice as you blow by and slam on the brakes in front of them...<BR>Of course, all this activity does get reported to the police over time, so then YOU are under survailence whenever YOU drive...<BR>Better to just hang back when you see someone at the corners waiting to turn, and there are no cars behind you, as they WILL turn in front of you...<BR>Then start following them home, and when they get home, slowly drive by stairing at the driver...<BR>I have had people freak out and try to get away, only to hit another car, then drive by smiling and wave!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||08-03-2001||10:17 AM||||think twice about putting any horn on your Fiero that doenst sound like a car horn<P>I had a friend in Miami who got tired of people always pulling out in front of him on his Harley, so he got this big electric horn that sounded like a truck.<P>  some greyhead lady started pulling out on him in a caddy, while he was doing 60, he nails the horn, she stops for a second, doesnt see no truck, and then pulls out in front of him anyway.<P>  he T boned her at about 55, was thrown into some bushes and was ok, totalled his bike. The lady was yelling at the cops "those motorcycles are dangerous - they shouldnt be allowed on the streets!"<P>  the problem with Fieros is the small front profile and we are low to the ground - spend your money on a set of driving lights, or daytime running lights - they are proven to be effective under all conditions - they really work.<P>  If you do get louder horns, make sure they still sound like a car - get a set off an old Crown Victoria or an old Buick.<P>  the problem with the horn solution is you have to watch the wheels of cars that are waiting to pull out, and its really hard to tell if they are only creeping up to the intersection, or if they dont see you and are pulling out. By the time you realize they are pulling out hitting the horn is too late.<P>  [But personally - I lean on the horn and cover the brake with my foot everytime I see someone creeping up to the intersection - they are required by law to stop and stay stopped until there is nothing coming - and I have no way of knowing if they see me or not].<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 08-03-2001).]||||reg||10
